{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1476541038,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxODMyMTE4ODc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1021","origin":"github"},"title":"RFC: ENH: create --to-annex-scheme  to set a policy which files are (not) added to annex","message":"in light of #1019 I wondered if we should add an option to `create` which would provide a few choices for default behavior of \"add/save\" -- what files should go to annex. I see a few possible schemes we could easily set:\n- **all** -- that is what we have ATM. no .gitattributes generated, everything goes to annex unless explicitly aid to go to git\n- **largenontext** -- which would generate .gitattributes\n\n``` shell\n* annex.largefiles=(largerthan=100kb and not (mimetype=text/*))\n```\n- **nontext** -- I think this is what should be our default, and which would generate .gitattributes\n\n``` shell\n* annex.largefiles=not (mimetype=text/*)\n```\n\nI haven't tried those specific values for largefiles yet, but according to https://git-annex.branchable.com/tips/largefiles/  should work, right @joeyh ?\n\npossibly relates to #925 (create-sibling), #996 (`add --to=git|annex`) ...","files":null}]}